-- title:
--   Full Slice Scalar Marginalize X
-- statement:
--   **First-term switch-sandwich comparison between full and evaluated slices.**
--
--   Let $S$ be a symmetric strategy with normalized state $\psi$, and let $G^x$ be the projective polynomial measurement at slice height $x$. Assume the slice family is strongly self-consistent with error $\zeta$. The full-slice cubic average sums the expectation of the ordered product of the two slice effects over uniform heights $x,y\in\mathbb{F}_q$ and polynomial outcomes, while the evaluated-slice cubic average evaluates those outcomes at uniformly sampled ambient points. Then
--
--   $$
--   \left|\operatorname{fullSliceABAAvg}(S,G)-\operatorname{evaluatedSliceABAAvg}(S,G)\right|\le 4\sqrt{\zeta}.
--   $$
--
--   The proof compares both averages with the same switch-sandwich center. This is the first scalar marginalization estimate used by `fullSliceCommutation_of_evaluated_on_evaluated_questions`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.fullSlice_scalar_marginalize_x`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
